{"t": 1794116952.6152735, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change (commit 8c2f1d0) introduced a reconciliation bug in production: converting with `int(amount_minor * rate)` truncates instead of rounding, so converted totals come out 1 minor unit low (e.g. expected 1100, got 1099).\n\nSentry issue: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ \u2014 `ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit`, first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3, ~2,201 events.\n\nFix: restore half-up rounding via `Decimal.quantize(Decimal(\"1\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)` in `worker/rates.py`.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
